{"timestamp":"1725320776","author":"🐶","location":{"commit":"6ef07cd52802635f87acc1286be07ccb2d0e6d92"},"description":"This is the commit header, it shows a hash which uniquely identifies the\ncommit, and the author of the commit. In this case, I have just used emojis to\nrepresent the different people who are part of the book: 🐶 is the person\nwriting code, and 🐱 is the person asking questions about the code.\n"}

{"timestamp":"1725440587","author":"🐶","location":{"commit":"6ef07cd52802635f87acc1286be07ccb2d0e6d92","range":{"startLine":1}},"description":"The first line of the commit message is called the subject, and conventionally\nit should be under 50 characters long, but this is not a limit.\n"}

{"timestamp":"1725476451","author":"🐶","location":{"commit":"6ef07cd52802635f87acc1286be07ccb2d0e6d92","path":".editorconfig","range":{"startLine":0}},"description":"This is the file called `.editorconfig`. The line starting with `@@` is not part of the file, it is called the \"diff hunk header\". In this case it just says we are adding lines 1 to 13 to a new file:\n- the `-0,0` means the file previously had no content;\n- the `+1,13` means the hunk spans from line 1 to 13 lines below (including line 1)."}

{"timestamp":"1726328537","author":"🐶","location":{"commit":"6ef07cd52802635f87acc1286be07ccb2d0e6d92","path":".editorconfig","range":{"startLine":1}},"description":"This is the first line of the newly added file. Note, that the '+' is not part of the line, it is there to indicate that this is a newly added line."}
